// REJECTS: Unexpected token 'ingestMode'. Valid alternatives: ['sink']
//
// `streamingPersister: PERSISTER_STREAMING BRACE_OPEN (persisterSink)* BRACE_CLOSE` -- a
// sink and nothing else. Batch and Streaming share the `persister:` keyword and the sink
// sub-block, and differ only in which further blocks are legal, so this is the near-miss
// that tells the two apart.
//
// Unlike most of this grammar's constraints, this one IS in the .g4, which is why it fails
// at parse time rather than in the walker. The ingest mode is written before the sink so
// that the expected set ANTLR reports is the one-element set that makes the point.
###Persistence
Persistence test::persistence::neg::StreamingWithIngestMode
{
  doc: 'streaming persister carrying a batch ingest mode';
  trigger: Manual;
  service: test::persistence::Service;
  persister: Streaming
  {
    ingestMode: NontemporalSnapshot
    {
      auditing: None;
    }
    sink: Relational
    {
      database: test::persistence::Database;
    }
  }
}
